# Cloudflare Pages reads this file to attach response headers to every
# request for the frontend. The API (Railway) already gets a solid default
# set from helmet() in server/src/app.js — this is the frontend's equivalent,
# which had none at all before this file existed.
#
# Deliberately NOT a Content-Security-Policy: this site loads scripts from
# multiple external origins (Clerk's CDN, cdnjs for chess.js) and runs a
# WASM chess engine via a Web Worker (engine/), each of which needs its own
# careful CSP allowance (script-src, worker-src, wasm-unsafe-eval, connect-src
# for api.usecheese.xyz). Getting that wrong fails closed — a misconfigured
# CSP can silently blank the whole app or break Stockfish/Clerk — so it needs
# its own dedicated pass with real testing across every page, not a header
# bolted on during an audit. The headers below carry no such risk: none of
# them restrict what the page is allowed to load.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
